# Datasets. These live outside the repo in C:\Users\yusuf\amc-data -- around
# 40 GB across the original HDF5 and the .npy memmaps converted from it. Not
# ours to redistribute, and far past what git should hold.
*.npy
*.hdf5
*.h5
*.pkl

# Trained weights. Regenerable by rerunning the scripts, and a fresh binary
# blob on every run, so committing them would bloat the history with churn
# that nobody ever reads a diff of.
*.pt

# Papers. Copyrighted PDFs and the text/figures extracted from them -- fine to
# keep on disk for reference, not to publish in a repository.
papers/

# Run logs. Raw stdout, superseded by the .json and .npz result files that the
# scripts write alongside them.
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.bak

# What is deliberately NOT ignored, since the reasoning matters:
#   *.npz, *.json   experiment results -- small (about 100 KB in total) and
#                   the actual record of what was measured. A result nobody
#                   can look up later is a result nobody can check.
#   figures/        the plots are the output of this project, not a build
#                   artifact, and they are what gets read first.

# Superseded IQNet-era results and the README that quoted them. Kept on disk
# so nothing is lost, kept out of the repository so a fresh session does not
# mistake them for current measurements.
archive_iqnet/

# Private working material: meeting notes, slide decks and study pages. Kept
# on disk, out of the public repository.
deck/
MEETING_*
CALL_*
KAM_NOTES.md
READING_LIST.md
